# Passwordless sudo for vpnCLI (openvpn backend) — GENERATED, do not edit by hand.
#
# `vpnctl install-sudoers` renders this template with the values detected on
# THIS machine (user, helper, openvpn path, config path, auth-file path, pid path)
# when VPN_TYPE=openvpn, and installs the result to the configured sudoers
# path, suffixed for this backend (default /etc/sudoers.d/vpncli-openvpn —
# see ACTIVE_SUDOERS_PATH), so it never clobbers the fortivpn backend's own
# rule file, validated with `visudo -cf`.
#
# Passwordless sudo only applies to the EXACT command lines below. All commands
# are rendered from the same paths the tool actually runs, so:
#   - the helper starts and supervises the VPN process,
#   - status verifies the PID belongs to the expected VPN command, and
#   - stop terminates only the PID recorded by the root-owned helper.
# Because it is generated per machine, moving the repo can never desync it.
#
# The auth-file path is fixed (state dir) and its contents are rewritten fresh
# (username + password from the secret store) before every launch — it is
# never committed and never appears on the command line's argv, only as a
# --auth-user-pass FILE reference.
#
# Re-run `vpnctl install-sudoers` after changing the openvpn path or the
# config location.

__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: __HELPER__ start-openvpn __OPENVPN__ __OVPN_CONFIG__ __AUTH_FILE__ __PID_FILE__
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: __HELPER__ status __OPENVPN__ __OVPN_CONFIG__ __PID_FILE__
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: __HELPER__ stop __PID_FILE__
